---
import DocsNav from "../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { evidenceHighlights, evidenceLevels, repositoryUrl } from "../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Evidence | Loom Infer"
  description="Bounded correctness and performance records for Loom Infer providers."
  active="Evidence"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Evidence</p>
    <h1>Each result keeps its boundary.</h1>
    <p>
      A result fixes the source, hardware, contract, baseline, method, and
      excluded claims.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Evidence" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Evidence levels</h2>
      <div class="evidence-level-grid">
        {evidenceLevels.map((item) => (
          <div class="evidence-level-card">
            <span>{item.level}</span>
            <div><h3>{item.name}</h3><p>{item.detail}</p></div>
            <small>{item.status}</small>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <h2>Current evidence status</h2>
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Result</th><th>Direction</th><th>Contract</th><th>Boundary</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {evidenceHighlights.map((item) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{item.value}</td>
              <td>{item.label}</td>
              <td>{item.detail}</td>
              <td>{item.sample}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="doc-note warning">
        <strong>The merged CUDA source requires requalification.</strong>
        <p>
          DeviceRegion changed the submission path for every provider. The
          published device, Graph, and performance records cover earlier source
          trees. They remain historical records for those exact trees.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Long paged prefill has two token-parallel providers.</strong>
        <p>
          The merged source selects sixteen warps for long MQA and eight warps
          for long GQA4. The incoming records passed the H20 CPU oracle and four
          Compute Sanitizer tools before the DeviceRegion merge.
        </p>
        <p>
          Those records do not qualify the merged source. Correctness,
          sanitizer, and matched performance require a new run before Loom can
          publish a current provider ranking.
        </p>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/h20-bf16-paged-prefill-token-parallel-correctness-20260807.json`}>
          Historical token-parallel correctness record
        </a>
        <span> · </span>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/h20-flashinfer-v0.6.16.post1-paged-prefill-long-eager-performance-20260807.json`}>
          Historical long-context performance record
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Fused append now uses a checked three-command path.</strong>
        <p>
          One validator builds a cache-bound append map. The mapped kernel then
          rotates Q and K and writes private K/V pages. A device-status copy
          reports semantic rejection at completion.
        </p>
        <p>
          The 2026-08-06 append records measured the earlier single-kernel path
          without exclusive-page ownership or typed status. They do not support
          a current performance or Graph claim.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Current exclusions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No result proves model or serving speedup.</li>
        <li>Eager provider timing is not isolated kernel timing.</li>
        <li>Graph results cover fixed addresses and named paths only.</li>
        <li>H20 results do not qualify other GPU architectures.</li>
        <li>One shape does not establish a universal provider winner.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Read the complete <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/README.md`}>evidence index</a>
        for source hashes, fixtures, raw samples, and exclusions.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
